// A file-level function whose name begins with `_` is callable from inside any
// block. GUIDE.md § 4 gives `_` exact block scope over *variables*; a function
// declaration is not one. BUG-GOL-002 (GoL/HALLAZGOS.md): the browser engine
// applied the variable rule to the function namespace, in both its analyzer and
// its runtime, so no script with a `_private()` helper ran in the playground.
//
// The variable half of the rule stands and is not tested here: `_v = 5` read
// from inside `@ 1 { }` is still refused by all three engines.

_uno() { <~ 1 }
_doble(x) { <~ x * 2 }

>> "top level: " _uno() ¶
@ 1 { >> "inside a loop: " _uno() ¶ }
? #1 { >> "inside an if: " _doble(_uno()) ¶ }
externa() { <~ _uno() + 10 }
>> "from a function: " externa() ¶
@ i:1..2 {
    @ _j:1..1 { >> "nested: " _doble(i) ¶ }
}
